    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d613">

                <pb facs="0775" n="701" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg701"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/5450</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Reinsch</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-11-17T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 17, 1917, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your November 10, 12 noon. Please inform Department what is meant by economic
                    blockade of the Central powers. The Department in its telegram of September 20,
                    4 p.m.,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d613-f1"/> in reply to yours of September 5,
                        midnight,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d613-f2"/> explained that it was impossible
                    to accede to certain measures proposed by other powers.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
